1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:07,765
Tesla wanted more. In Colorado he built a giant coil and produced lightning bolts over a hundred feet long.

2
00:00:07,985 --> 00:00:16,062
One night he burned out the power company's generator… and the town went dark. He had to pay for the repairs.

3
00:00:16,262 --> 00:00:24,262
That's where his most famous photo comes from, reading calmly beside giant lightning bolts. It's a trick: two photos superimposed.

4
00:00:24,462 --> 00:00:31,155
Later, banker J. P. Morgan gave him a hundred and fifty thousand dollars to build a tower.

5
00:00:31,355 --> 00:00:39,585
Morgan wanted wireless messages. Tesla dreamed of something bigger: wireless power for the entire planet.

6
00:00:39,785 --> 00:00:46,939
But Marconi crossed the Atlantic with a radio signal and simpler equipment. Morgan put up no more money.

7
00:00:47,389 --> 00:00:56,543
The tower never worked. And physics wasn't helping: wireless energy spreads out in every direction, like light from a lamp.

8
00:00:56,743 --> 00:01:02,512
The farther you go, the less arrives. Across a few centimeters, however, it works very well.

9
00:01:03,412 --> 00:01:09,181
His wireless energy exists. It reaches a few centimeters and charges your phone.
